    false - it is a psychic R.C.C. and states no S.D.C. or hit point formula
    (Psyscape p.54 heading "Mind Bleeder Psychic R.C.C.").
  - Power ladder (p.53, abilities 4 and 5): four Mind Bleeder powers at level
    1, two more at levels 3, 6, 8, 10 and 12; three from Healing, Sensitive or
    Physical at levels 2 and 4; one Super-Psionic at levels 3, 7, 11 and 15.
    Judgement call: the book says the three at levels 2 and 4 come "from one of
    the following categories", read here as all three from a single category.
    The catalog cannot enforce a same-category rule, so each grant offers all
    three categories and the note tells the player. The class has NO automatic
    catalog powers; Sense Psionics and Mind Bleed are R.C.C. abilities, not
    psionic_powers rows, and are special_abilities.
  - Psi-Bonuses (p.53 #6): +2 to save vs psionics stored as saves.psionics; the
    book says M.E. attribute bonuses do NOT apply to this save. Not stored as a
    separate rule; stated in the Psi-Bonuses special ability.
  - R.C.C. Bonuses (p.53 #9): "+4 to save vs magic or chemical mind control"
    stored as mind_control 4; "+4 vs magic illusions" as illusionary_magic 4.
  - Ley line influence (p.53 #3) is conditional on location and is in GM Notes.
  - Languages: "Speaks Euro and native language at 96%" stored as Language:
    Euro and Language: Native Tongue at 96 with no per-level gain. "Pilot
    Hovercraft" is the catalog''s Hover Craft (ground). Fixed skills fold the
    printed bonus into the catalog base (Climbing 40+5=45).
  - R.C.C. Related: 9 picks (three Physical or Rogue, three Espionage or
    Wilderness, three any other), stored as count 9 with two union minimums.
    "Other" skills in the hand to hand line read as R.C.C. Related picks.
  - Secondary skills: six, no later-level additions printed.
  - Money (p.55): 1D6x1000 credits (cache shows "!D6xlOOO", the known digit
    fault; render confirms 1D6x1000). Also starts with 3D6x1000 in salable
    Black Market items, which starting_money cannot hold; noted here. The book
    adds that a Mind Bleeder can often earn big money as a spy.
  - Equipment (p.55): "any light to heavy mega-damage armor" enumerated as
    generic Rifts armor rows; "a couple sets of clothing" as 2 traveling
    clothes; "a knife or two" stored as one knife; "1D6 E-clips for each"
    (pistol and rifle) stored as one e-clip entry of 2d6; "personal items" not
    stored. The book adds that Mind Bleeders like magic weapons and devices of
    all kinds, particularly Techno-Wizard devices - no starting item implied.
  - Alignment: any, though most are Anarchist (40%) or evil (35%); good or
    Unprincipled Mind Bleeders are rare and scorned by their own kind.
    Attribute requirements: none, but M.E. 10+ strongly suggested. Neither is
    a schema restriction; recorded here.
  - Physical description (p.52): human-looking, average height 6 to 6.5 feet
    (1.8-1.95 m); only tell is swelling, pulsing veins in the head when using
    psionics.
---

## Lore

The Mind Bleeder is a D-bee race, nearly indistinguishable from humans until its powers are used, when the veins of the head bulge and pulse and the face flushes. The name comes from its knack for "bleeding" thoughts, skills and psychic energy out of others, and from the tiny hemorrhages its neurological attacks leave in a victim''s brain. The race came through rifts around the Mediterranean roughly a century ago and now numbers perhaps half a million to a million across North Africa and southern Europe, with smaller pockets elsewhere; the NGR and Triax use them as spies but never trust them, and the Splugorth now recruit them in Atlantis. Raised in clannish families that teach them they are superior to other races, most are opportunists, con artists and schemers who read minds and meddle without a second thought. Psi-Stalkers, Dog Boys and Nega-Psychics treat them as natural enemies, and most people regard them as dangerous parasites.

## GM Notes

**Power selection by level** (Psyscape p.53):

- **1st level:** four Mind Bleeder powers.
- **2nd and 4th level:** a total of three powers from one of Healing, Sensitive or Physical.
- **3rd, 7th, 11th and 15th level:** one Super-Psionic power.
- **3rd, 6th, 8th, 10th and 12th level:** two more Mind Bleeder powers.

The Mind Bleeder''s own I.S.P. (M.E. + 10, +2D4 per level) is small by design; it relies on Mind Bleed to fuel its powers from other psychics.

**Ley line influence:** range and duration of psychic abilities +25% near a ley line and +50% within one mile (1.6 km) of a nexus. Damage from the Bleeder''s psionic energy and neurological attacks (Psi-Sword, Pyrokinesis, Electrokinesis, Telekinesis and the like) is doubled within one mile of a nexus.
